            <ArticleTitle>[Immunopharmacological activity of xymedone in patients with atopic bronchial asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>31-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Xymedone produced therapeutic effect in patients with atopic bronchial asthma. The drug action was manifested by a decrease in the IgE level and an increase in gamma-interferon level. Adding xymedone to lymphocytes cultivated with phytohemagglutinin revealed stimulating action of this drug on the delayed-type hypersensitivity. Mechanisms involved in the immunotropic action of xymedone are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
